Input: goodix-berlin: decode Samsung GT6936 coordinate events

Samsung GT6936 firmware emits 16-byte SEC coordinate records while its
IC_INFO may advertise the reference 8-byte point size. The unmodified
Berlin driver consequently treats contact data as a checksum and drops
all touches. Select the vendor layout by firmware PID, validate its
header/point metadata and decode packed 12-bit positions and releases.

Keep the existing 8-byte layout and two-contact pre-read for other
controllers. Samsung uses a one-contact initial transfer (26 bytes) and
reads further contacts from the exact continuation offset. Preserve the
original technical description of standard packet reads.

Adapted from the Tab S9 Ultra port's Samsung event patch, with firmware-
scoped layout selection, unchanged standard pre-read and indexed point
iteration so unsupported contacts do not repeat the previous record:
https://github.com/agcarbajo/postmarketos-galaxy-tab-s9-ultra/blob/b1dcca03fdc7952de60c3e9ab49e860b6bd45e8c/pmaports/device/testing/linux-samsung-gts9uwifi-mainline/support-samsung-goodix-16-byte-events.patch

Generated from the pinned Linux 7.2 driver. Drop when upstream Berlin
supports this firmware layout; no corresponding upstream commit known.

